{title: My Savior First of All}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / John R. Sweney}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Sacred Songs No. 1, by Ira D. Sankey, James McGranahan & George C. Stebbins (New York: Biglow & Main, 1896), # 126)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]When my life work is ended,
[G]And I cross the [C]swelling [G]tide,
[G]When the bright and glorious morning [F#m]I shall [D]see;
[G]I shall know my Redeemer
[G]When I [C]reach the other side,
[C]And His [G]smile will [D7]be the first to welcome [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]I shall know__[D7]__ Him, I shall [G]know Him,
[G]And redeemed by His side [F#m]I shall [D]stand,
[D]I shall [G]know Him, I shall [Am]know [C]Him,
[C]By the [G]print [D7]of the nails in His [G]hand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Oh, the soul thrilling rapture
[G]When I view His [C]blessèd [G]face,
[G]And the luster of His kindly [F#m]beaming [D]eye;
[G]How my full heart will praise Him
[G]For the [C]mercy, love and grace,
[C]That pre[G]pare for [D7]me a mansion in the [G]sky.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Oh, the dear ones in glory,
[G]How they beckon [C]me to [G]come,
[G]And our parting at the river [F#m]I re[D]call;
[G]To the sweet vales of Eden
[G]They will [C]sing my welcome home;
[C]But I [G]long to [D7]meet my Savior first of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Through the gates to the city
[G]In a robe of [C]spotless [G]white,
[G]He will lead me where no tears will [F#m]ever [D]fall;
[G]In the glad song of ages
[G]I shall [C]mingle with delight;
[C]But I [G]long to [D7]meet my Savior first of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
